# FIX-168: boot-config readers of live-settings sections that are correct as they are, one
# `section.key reason` per line. Ratchet: an entry nobody reads fails the guard.
# Deliberately not listed because not live: `ssh.*` (`ssh/plane.rs`, `ssh/sessions.rs`,
# `settings/service.rs` `check_ssh_needs_terminal`) is a startup-only key (D-358): no `ssh.` key is in
# the settings registry or in `install_live_ops`'s PREFIXES, so reading `config.ssh.enabled` is right.
# Should `ssh.` ever become live, the guard picks it up from PREFIXES and these readers must move.
previews.enabled configuration-only (NOT_SETTINGS, settings.rs)
previews.domain configuration-only (NOT_SETTINGS, settings.rs)
